WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.990 --> 00:00:04.440
My own token, against
the entitlements API.

2
00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:08.350
401. One command later, the same call:

3
00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:12.200
200. Nothing changed in the token.

4
00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:15.320
Something changed in who
the stack thinks I am.

5
00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:25.020
Fieldnote nine. Who is asking.

6
00:00:26.054 --> 00:00:28.864
Who does the stack think you
are, and what may you do?

7
00:00:30.438 --> 00:00:32.928
Your own Azure token gets
you through the mesh.

8
00:00:33.238 --> 00:00:36.198
spi users puts you in entitlements groups,

9
00:00:36.198 --> 00:00:38.678
and the role you choose
decides what you may do,

10
00:00:38.678 --> 00:00:41.168
including whether
Workflow may act for you.

11
00:00:43.162 --> 00:00:47.332
spi token --me prints
your own Azure token.

12
00:00:47.722 --> 00:00:52.122
The mesh accepts its issuer, and the
sidecar in front of each service writes your

13
00:00:52.122 --> 00:00:53.732
unique_name as the caller.

14
00:00:54.042 --> 00:00:55.882
Then entitlements looks you up.

15
00:00:55.882 --> 00:00:59.562
Bring-up seeded three
identities, the workload,

16
00:00:59.562 --> 00:01:03.132
the deploy identity and the
member, and nobody else.

17
00:01:03.322 --> 00:01:09.202
So you get 401. Plain spi token
mints the deploy identity instead,

18
00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:10.842
which is why it always worked:

19
00:01:10.842 --> 00:01:12.852
every call was the platform's.

20
00:01:15.086 --> 00:01:20.766
spi users add --me reads your token
and applies the mesh's own claim

21
00:01:20.766 --> 00:01:23.896
order, so it stores the
id entitlements will see.

22
00:01:24.606 --> 00:01:28.216
The deploy identity writes the
groups, because it sits in ops.

23
00:01:28.606 --> 00:01:31.166
Then the command calls
entitlements with your token,

24
00:01:31.166 --> 00:01:33.016
and keeps trying for up to a minute.

25
00:01:33.246 --> 00:01:37.416
Here, it answered, and the
same curl returned 200.

26
00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:42.196
A role is a preset of groups.

27
00:01:42.746 --> 00:01:45.396
Viewer is users and datalake viewers.

28
00:01:45.866 --> 00:01:48.906
Editor, admin and ops
each add impersonation,

29
00:01:48.906 --> 00:01:52.916
which lets the stack's OSDU identity
act for you through Workflow.

30
00:01:53.786 --> 00:01:57.706
As a viewer, the ingestion smoke
refused before any run started:

31
00:01:57.706 --> 00:01:59.396
impersonation missing.

32
00:01:59.946 --> 00:02:02.276
As an editor, it can run as you.

33
00:02:04.854 --> 00:02:06.144
Follow your own call.

34
00:02:06.294 --> 00:02:10.694
Your token passes the mesh, and the
sidecar writes your unique_name.

35
00:02:10.694 --> 00:02:13.984
Entitlements finds no group, and refuses.

36
00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:17.414
spi users add puts you in
users and a role's groups,

37
00:02:17.414 --> 00:02:20.864
written by the deploy identity,
and checks with your token.

38
00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:23.504
Entitlements finds you now.

39
00:02:23.894 --> 00:02:27.504
Same token, same call, 200.

40
00:02:30.298 --> 00:02:31.548
An easy mistake:

41
00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:35.378
running spi users add again
adds to the role I hold.

42
00:02:35.378 --> 00:02:39.228
It replaces it. Here,
viewer became editor.

43
00:02:39.298 --> 00:02:42.978
Users stayed. Editors and
impersonation were added,

44
00:02:42.978 --> 00:02:45.068
and datalake viewers was removed.

45
00:02:45.538 --> 00:02:48.258
Going back to viewer
removes impersonation too,

46
00:02:48.258 --> 00:02:50.268
and ingestion as you stops.

47
00:02:50.498 --> 00:02:52.748
Check with spi users list.

48
00:02:55.334 --> 00:02:56.624
So now you can say:

49
00:02:56.774 --> 00:03:01.504
your own token passes the
mesh, and entitlements decides.

50
00:03:02.054 --> 00:03:06.384
spi users stores the id the
mesh writes, and proves it.

51
00:03:06.534 --> 00:03:10.704
And only editor, admin and
ops can run ingestion as you.

52
00:03:13.166 --> 00:03:17.566
Next: when is a new environment
ready, open for deploys,

53
00:03:17.566 --> 00:03:18.936
and holding data?

